# PRIVATE LAYER — recruiter-readiness cleanup 2026-06-10
# Personal/job-hunt material lives on local disk, never on GitHub.
# History scrubbed via git filter-repo (see docs/2026-06-10-code-brain-
# recruiter-readiness-audit-plan.md). Agents must never `git add` these.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Job-hunt command center — consolidated private home.
# Runtime writers: job_feed.py, daily_driver.py, mock_interview_loop.py,
# substack_drafter.py (paths unchanged; they read/write on-disk, not via git).
vault/20_projects/prj-job-hunt-2026/
# 2026-08 revamp home (resumes, campaign strategy) — same private class as above.
vault/20_projects/prj-job-hunt-2026-REVAMP/

# Job-feed run manifests — added 2026-08-11 after an independent privacy pass.
# These were TRACKED AND PUSHED, and their runs[].failed_pollers entries name
# target companies as literal `ats:<slug>` values — 69 distinct companies, i.e.
# the whole watchlist above, leaked through a side channel while watchlist.yaml
# itself was correctly ignored. The fleet board reads these from disk
# (build.py: VAULT = Path.home()/"Code-Brain/code-brain/vault"), never from git,
# so untracking them costs the board nothing. History scrubbed the same day.
vault/health/job-feed-manifest-*.json

# Substack Studio private lane — the project at vault/20_projects/substack-studio/ is TRACKED
